			<div class="content" id="post-content-4501831">
									

<p>Overall, I found this article to be enjoyable, and it has quite the potential indeed. I don’t think this is a bad piece, but I feel it still has some stuff that needs addressing.<br />
Firstly, I don’t really get the object classification. I don’t see a reason for this SCP to be a Keter, and for the Foundation to have such a hard time redacting and censoring it. The risk class and notice class also seem a bit off; In my humble reader opinion, I think you should either make the object more containable or make the relation between the whole “entitlement and censorship” theme and the anomalous properties more obvious and logical to us readers.<br />
Also, just like gee0765 pointed out earlier, the ending is quite underwhelming. The AWCY? bit seems really artificial and lame. Maybe you could change the ending to focus more on the relationship between the two PoI, and an eventual fallout and maybe suicide as cause of the anomalous behavior. ( Note: this is just something I came up with on a whim. I’m certain you can probably figure something that better fits your style and objectives)<br />
In conclusion, I must say that while this article is still not SCP Foundation quality, its not THAT far from it. Anyway, this is all just this newbie’s opinion. I really hope your SCP grows and develops exponentially, DianaBerry!</p>

